<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Capitulations of Santa Fe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1492</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitulations-of-the-ottoman-empire">Capitulations</a> of Santa Fe were the agreement signed on 17 April 1492 at Santa Fe, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, between Isabella I and Ferdinand II and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a>. They granted Columbus the title of Admiral of the Ocean Sea, the offices of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> and governor of any lands he discovered, and a tenth of the profits. Disputes over these rights later led to long lawsuits between his heirs and the crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/capitulations-of-santa-fe.jpg" alt="Capitulations of Santa Fe" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: XpoferenS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Capitulacionsori.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
